  "source_sha256": "086e76486570e4154195d121c723c08f09e4a6539cea6136dcd572efd85160c5",
  "fragments": [
    {
      "id": "e_086e76486570_0001",
      "text": "Oracle Bypass via Stale Observation and Failure Fallback",
      "start": 0,
      "end": 56,
      "line": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "e_086e76486570_0002",
      "text": "## Finding description and impact",
      "start": 58,
      "end": 91,
      "line": 3
    },
    {
      "id": "e_086e76486570_0003",
      "text": "The protocol's safety reliance on `checkPoolAndGetCenterPrice` creates a false sense of security.",
      "start": 93,
      "end": 190,
      "line": 5
    },
    {
      "id": "e_086e76486570_0004",
      "text": "The `checkPoolAndGetCenterPrice` function contains a logic flaw where it returns `centerSqrtPriceX96` (Spot Price) directly, bypassing all deviation checks under two conditions:",
      "start": 194,
      "end": 371,
      "line": 8
    },
    {
      "id": "e_086e76486570_0005",
      "text": "*  1. When `oldestTimestamp + SECONDS_AGO < block.timestamp` (TWAP window expired).",
      "start": 373,
      "end": 456,
      "line": 10
    },
    {
      "id": "e_086e76486570_0006",
      "text": "*  2. When the oracle query fails (`!success`).",
      "start": 459,
      "end": 506,
      "line": 13
    },
    {
      "id": "e_086e76486570_0007",
      "text": "The protocol's safety reliance on `checkPoolAndGetCenterPrice` creates a false sense of security. The function contains a critical logic flaw where it silently falls back to the `centerSqrtPriceX96` (Spot Price), bypassing all deviation checks and providing any downstream contract (like `LiquidityManager`) with a poisoned baseline.",
      "start": 509,
      "end": 842,
      "line": 16
    },
    {
      "id": "e_086e76486570_0008",
      "text": "**1. The Vulnerable Oracle Logic (Silent Bypass)**",
      "start": 845,
      "end": 895,
      "line": 19
    },
    {
      "id": "e_086e76486570_0009",
      "text": "The internal logic contains two critical bypasses where it returns the manipulated `slot0` price instead of reverting on invalid or stale data:",
      "start": 897,
      "end": 1040,
      "line": 21
    },
    {
      "id": "e_086e76486570_0010",
      "text": "**2. Downstream Impact on Execution**",
      "start": 1043,
      "end": 1080,
      "line": 24
    },
    {
      "id": "e_086e76486570_0011",
      "text": "When the Oracle bypass occurs, the calling contract (the \"Victim\") receives the manipulated price as if it were a validated \"Center Price.\"",
      "start": 1082,
      "end": 1221,
      "line": 26
    },
    {
      "id": "e_086e76486570_0012",
      "text": "**Root Cause**",
      "start": 1224,
      "end": 1238,
      "line": 29
    },
    {
      "id": "e_086e76486570_0013",
      "text": "The fundamental issue is the non-linear relationship between `sqrtPriceX96` and actual price $P$.",
      "start": 1240,
      "end": 1337,
      "line": 31
    },
    {
      "id": "e_086e76486570_0014",
      "text": "Price Derivation: $P = (\\frac{sqrtPriceX96}{2^{96}})^2$",
      "start": 1339,
      "end": 1394,
      "line": 33
    },
    {
      "id": "e_086e76486570_0015",
      "text": "Deviation Calculation:",
      "start": 1396,
      "end": 1418,
      "line": 35
    },
    {
      "id": "e_086e76486570_0016",
      "text": "$$",
      "start": 1421,
      "end": 1423,
      "line": 37
    },
    {
      "id": "e_086e76486570_0017",
      "text": "\\Delta P = \\left( \\frac{\\text{sqrtPriceX96}_{spot}^{2}}{\\text{sqrtPriceX96}_{TWAP}^{2}} - 1 \\right) \\times 100\\%",
      "start": 1424,
      "end": 1536,
      "line": 38
    },
    {
      "id": "e_086e76486570_0018",
      "text": "$$",
      "start": 1537,
      "end": 1539,
      "line": 39
    }
  ]
}
